{"parentUuid":"112a8440-4f9e-4b42-93e5-242f75d3d0f1","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011krE3ZnsctSa4V3GWNFK2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Na7MywScbwopUYYKWcvWX","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"planar multi-commodity flow algorithm 2024 grid graph polynomial"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8681,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":290,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8681},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8681,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozcCaa4CW4KdfFcf7y6","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c472e5d4-83bc-4e2e-b97d-e116d3830ed9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:56.382Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"112a8440-4f9e-4b42-93e5-242f75d3d0f1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VpQPbmbLcE2m9Cco9TfQ2X","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Lipton-Tarjan planar separator practical implementation 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Separator Theorem for Planar Graphs | SIAM Journal on Applied Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://epubs.siam.org/doi/abs/10.1137/0136016\"},{\"title\":\"Applications of a Planar Separator Theorem | SIAM Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/0209046\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jeffythedragonslayer/lipton-tarjan: Implementation of the Lipton-Tarjan separator algorithm for planar graphs\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jeffythedragonslayer/lipton-tarjan\"},{\"title\":\"Planar separator theorem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planar_separator_theorem\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan: Python implementation of Lipton-Tarjan algorithm for planar separation\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 16 Planar separator By Sariel Har-Peled, January 16, 2025①\",\"url\":\"https://sarielhp.org/book/chapters/separator.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"lipton_tarjan/README.md at master · ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Applications of the Lipton and Tarjan's Planar Separator Theorem (Applied Combinatorial Theory and Algorithms)\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/277042708_Applications_of_the_Lipton_and_Tarjan's_Planar_Separator_Theorem_Applied_Combinatorial_Theory_and_Algorithms\"},{\"title\":\"lipton-tarjan/lipton-tarjan.cpp at master · jeffythedragonslayer/lipton-tarjan\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jeffythedragonslayer/lipton-tarjan/blob/master/lipton-tarjan.cpp\"},{\"title\":\"15-853 Page1 15-853:Algorithms in the Real World Planar Separators I & II\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/afs/cs/project/pscico-guyb/realworld/www/slidesF06/planarity-annotated.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Lipton-Tarjan planar separator practical implementations:\n\n## Theoretical Foundation\n\nThe Lipton-Tarjan theorem partitions an n-vertex planar graph into three sets where no edges connect the first two sets, neither contains more than 2n/3 vertices, and the separator contains at most 2√2√n vertices, with an algorithm that finds such a partition in O(n) time.\n\n## Recent Practical Implementations\n\nSeveral open-source implementations are available:\n\n1. **C++ Implementation**: A GitHub project implements the 1977 linear-time Lipton-Tarjan planar separator algorithm, finding a partition where the separator set partitions the graph roughly in half with no edges directly between the two main components. This implementation is built on top of the Boost Graph Library.\n\n2. **Python Implementation**: An algorithm computes the partitioning in O(n) time, with a dedicated Python implementation available. The Python version includes tests validating correctness on randomly generated planar graphs and demonstrates that execution time is linear.\n\n## Modern Research\n\nLipton and Tarjan presented an optimal separator of size O(√n). More recent work has explored variations and improvements to the algorithm. It is possible to construct an entire separator hierarchy in linear time by using the Lipton–Tarjan breadth-first layering approach with appropriate data structures.\n\n## Applications\n\nSeparator hierarchies can be used to devise efficient divide and conquer algorithms for planar graphs, and dynamic programming on these hierarchies can be used for NP-hard optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0be21894-049a-4aa2-a0b2-5f4945d281b0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:02.888Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"112a8440-4f9e-4b42-93e5-242f75d3d0f1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c472e5d4-83bc-4e2e-b97d-e116d3830ed9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Na7MywScbwopUYYKWcvWX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"planar multi-commodity flow algorithm 2024 grid graph polynomial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An Efficient Algorithm for Finding Multicommodity Flows in Planar Networks | SIAM Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://epubs.siam.org/doi/10.1137/0214023\"},{\"title\":\"Algorithms for multicommodity flows in planar graphs | Algorithmica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/BF01553903.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Multicommodity Max-Flow Min-Cut Theorems and Their ...\",\"url\":\"https://snap.stanford.edu/class/cs224w-readings/leighton99mincut.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Integer Multiflows in Acyclic Planar Digraphs | Combinatorica\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00493-023-00065-0\"},{\"title\":\"Multicommodity Flows in Even, Planar Networks | Algorithmica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/PL00009161\"},{\"title\":\"Multicommodity flows in certain planar directed networks - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0166218X9090134X\"},{\"title\":\"The All-or-Nothing Multicommodity Flow Problem - UPenn CIS\",\"url\":\"https://www.cis.upenn.edu/~sanjeev/papers/sicomp13_ANF.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Multicommodity flows in planar graphs - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0095895681800123\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Leveling the Grid | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Leveling-the-Grid-Cornelsen-Karrenbauer/e7d400a6a950b00789e6914c6209932ff3fb710e\"},{\"title\":\"On Constant Multi-Commodity Flow-Cut Gaps for Families ...\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10099098\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here are the key findings related to planar multi-commodity flow algorithms:\n\n## Classical Algorithms\n\nAn efficient algorithm for finding multicommodity flows in planar graphs spends O(kn + n² (log n)^1/2) time and O(kn) space if the graph has n vertices and k source–sink pairs.\n\nFor integral multicommodity flows in planar, undirected graphs where all sources and targets are on the boundary of the infinite face with evenness conditions on capacities and demands, an asymptotically optimal algorithm requires only O(kn) time in the worst case.\n\n## Special Graph Classes\n\nEfficient algorithms exist for the multicommodity flow problem on specific classes of planar undirected graphs, running in O(kn + nT(n)) time where T(n) is the time required for finding single-source shortest paths.\n\nFor capacity balanced directed planar networks, an O(K|V|) time graph theoretic algorithm tests feasibility of the multicommodity flow problem.\n\n## Recent Work (2023)\n\nA recent algorithm with complexity O((R+1)^(4k²) k³ n) solves the integer multiflow problem on acyclic planar digraphs, providing a polynomial-time algorithm for the arc-disjoint paths problem when k is fixed.\n\nThe search results show substantial classical work on planar multicommodity flows with polynomial-time algorithms, though I did not find specific 2024 results focused on grid graphs in the search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dd2f1ffe-5b96-46ab-b840-86d9647dc2e5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:05.586Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c472e5d4-83bc-4e2e-b97d-e116d3830ed9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
