{"parentUuid":"56ace838-baf3-4501-aafc-a3572159fc79","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RLoArsqoLQh5oHTZF9NMnu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HA6gwfniheZAae5aWG9AH6","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OGDF library planar separator algorithm Python binding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3221,"cache_read_input_tokens":24919,"output_tokens":330,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3221},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":330,"cache_read_input_tokens":24919,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3221,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozeSRaAXrFYeSjpxtND","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8357c6e1-91d6-4332-894c-286d8ac59ce5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:25.529Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"56ace838-baf3-4501-aafc-a3572159fc79","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YGYZ8UfWB7rZdtn9ivZvX5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NetworkX planar graph algorithms 2025 separator embedding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"networkx.algorithms.planarity.PlanarEmbedding — NetworkX 3.6.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/reference/algorithms/generated/networkx.algorithms.planarity.PlanarEmbedding.html\"},{\"title\":\"networkx.algorithms.planarity.PlanarEmbedding — NetworkX 3.5rc0.dev0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/latest/reference/algorithms/generated/networkx.algorithms.planarity.PlanarEmbedding.html\"},{\"title\":\"Algorithms — NetworkX 3.6.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/reference/algorithms/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"combinatorial_embedding_to_pos — NetworkX 3.6.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/reference/algorithms/generated/networkx.algorithms.planar_drawing.combinatorial_embedding_to_pos.html\"},{\"title\":\"networkx.algorithms.planar_drawing — NetworkX 3.6.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/_modules/networkx/algorithms/planar_drawing.html\"},{\"title\":\"Planarity — NetworkX 3.6.1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/reference/algorithms/planarity.html\"},{\"title\":\"networkx.algorithms.planar_drawing — NetworkX 3.7rc0.dev0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/latest/_modules/networkx/algorithms/planar_drawing.html\"},{\"title\":\"networkx.algorithms.planarity.check_planarity\",\"url\":\"https://pydocs.github.io/p/networkx/2.8.2/api/networkx.algorithms.planarity.check_planarity.html\"},{\"title\":\"Planarity — NetworkX 2.8 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/networkx-2.8/reference/algorithms/planarity.html\"},{\"title\":\"combinatorial_embedding_to_pos — NetworkX 3.4rc0.dev0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://networkx.org/documentation/latest/reference/algorithms/generated/networkx.algorithms.planar_drawing.combinatorial_embedding_to_pos.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about NetworkX planar graph algorithms:\n\n## NetworkX Planar Graph Algorithms\n\nNetworkX provides several key planar graph algorithms and utilities:\n\n### Core Planarity Functions\n\nThe `check_planarity` function checks if a graph is planar and returns a counterexample or an embedding. The planarity check algorithm and extraction of the combinatorial embedding is based on the Left-Right Planarity Test.\n\n### Planar Embedding\n\nThe PlanarEmbedding class is a subclass of nx.DiGraph that can still be used for algorithms requiring undirected graphs because the method is_directed() is overridden, and a valid PlanarGraph must have edges in both directions.\n\n### Planar Drawing\n\nThe algorithm for generating planar drawings iteratively inserts nodes of the input graph in a certain order and rearranges previously inserted nodes so that the planar drawing stays valid, which is done efficiently by only maintaining relative positions during node placements and calculating absolute positions at the end.\n\n**Note:** The search results show documentation for NetworkX versions up to 3.6-3.7, but there is no specific mention of \"separator\" algorithms in the results. The search may not have captured the full details on separator-based algorithms specifically. For the most current 2025 information, I'd recommend checking the official NetworkX documentation directly at networkx.org.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8278b440-3090-47c9-8253-92eaa774166e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:31.485Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"56ace838-baf3-4501-aafc-a3572159fc79","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8357c6e1-91d6-4332-894c-286d8ac59ce5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HA6gwfniheZAae5aWG9AH6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OGDF library planar separator algorithm Python binding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ogdf/ogdf-python: Automagic Python Bindings for the Open Graph Drawing Framework\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ogdf/ogdf-python\"},{\"title\":\"ogdf: Planar Separator Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://ogdf.github.io/doc/ogdf/group__ga-plansep.html\"},{\"title\":\"ogdf-python · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/ogdf-python/\"},{\"title\":\"OGDF – Open Graph Drawing Framework\",\"url\":\"https://ogdf.uos.de/\"},{\"title\":\"ogdf: ogdf::planar_separator::SeparatorDualHelper::CycleData Struct Reference\",\"url\":\"https://ogdf.github.io/doc/ogdf/structogdf_1_1planar__separator_1_1_separator_dual_helper_1_1_cycle_data.html\"},{\"title\":\"The Open Graph Drawing Framework (OGDF)\",\"url\":\"https://cs.brown.edu/people/rtamassi/gdhandbook/chapters/ogdf.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"release – OGDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.ogdf.uni-osnabrueck.de/category/release/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan: Python implementation of Lipton-Tarjan algorithm for planar separation\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan\"},{\"title\":\"grandalf · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/grandalf/\"},{\"title\":\"Open Graph Drawing Framework · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ogdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the OGDF library planar separator algorithm and Python bindings:\n\n## Python Bindings for OGDF\n\nogdf-python uses the cppyy library to automagically generate python bindings for the C++ Open Graph Drawing Framework (OGDF). It is available for Python>=3.6 and is Apache2 licensed.\n\n## Installation and Setup\n\nYou can use pip to install the ogdf-python package. You will need a local shared library build (-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON) of the OGDF. For easier setup, the optional [quickstart] pulls in matplotlib and jupyter lab as well as a ready-to-use binary build of the OGDF via ogdf-wheel.\n\n## Planar Separator Algorithms\n\nThe OGDF library includes functions for computing separators in planar graphs. The OGDF documentation provides detailed information about these planar separator algorithms, with specific implementations available through the C++ framework that are accessible via the Python bindings.\n\nTo use these features in Python, you would access the OGDF planar separator functions through the ogdf-python bindings after installation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8a476aa3-f986-48ad-8784-a9a4ec97224d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:34.322Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8357c6e1-91d6-4332-894c-286d8ac59ce5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8a476aa3-f986-48ad-8784-a9a4ec97224d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WbLaB3yUqyrLktWZjYUbPv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ULuQs176AeV4UauaupFxJz","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\routing_subproblem.py","offset":80,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5339,"cache_read_input_tokens":28140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5339,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":43,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozfUNgKjHfj7yviCNSA","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"268a46e6-7378-4d6f-90cb-6548df9e3013","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:38.186Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"268a46e6-7378-4d6f-90cb-6548df9e3013","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ULuQs176AeV4UauaupFxJz","type":"tool_result","content":"80\t            free_cells=free_cells,\n81\t            free_neighbors_by_cell=free_neighbors_by_cell,\n82\t            component_by_cell=component_by_cell,\n83\t            cells_by_component=cells_by_component,\n84\t        )\n85\t\n86\t\n87\tdef _dirs_tag(dirs: Iterable[str]) -> str:\n88\t    ordered = list(dirs)\n89\t    return \"\".join(ordered) if ordered else \"none\"\n90\t\n91\t\n92\tdef _is_straight_state(flow_in: Tuple[str, ...], flow_out: Tuple[str, ...]) -> bool:\n93\t    return (\n94\t        len(flow_in) == 1\n95\t        and len(flow_out) == 1\n96\t        and DIR_OPP[flow_in[0]] == flow_out[0]\n97\t    )\n98\t\n99\t\n100\tdef _sorted_cells(cells: Iterable[Tuple[int, int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n101\t    return [[int(x), int(y)] for x, y in sorted(cells)]\n102\t\n103\t\n104\tdef _cell_neighbors(cell: Tuple[int, int]) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:\n105\t    x, y = cell\n106\t    neighbors: List[Tuple[int, int]] = []\n107\t    for dx, dy in DIR_DELTA.values():\n108\t        nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n109\t        if 0 <= nx < GRID_W and 0 <= ny < GRID_H:\n110\t            neighbors.append((nx, ny))\n111\t    return neighbors\n112\t\n113\t\n114\tdef _compute_free_components(\n115\t    free_cells: Set[Tuple[int, int]],\n116\t    *,\n117\t    free_neighbors_by_cell: Optional[Mapping[Tuple[int, int], Sequence[Tuple[int, int]]]] = None,\n118\t) -> Tuple[Dict[Tuple[int, int], int], Dict[int, Set[Tuple[int, int]]]]:\n119\t    component_by_cell: Dict[Tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n120\t    cells_by_component: Dict[int, Set[Tuple[int, int]]] = {}\n121\t    component_id = 0\n122\t\n123\t    for cell in free_cells:\n124\t        if cell in component_by_cell:\n125\t            continue\n126\t        stack = [cell]\n127\t        component_by_cell[cell] = component_id\n128\t        component_cells: Set[Tuple[int, int]] = {cell}\n129\t        while stack:\n130\t            current = stack.pop()\n131\t            neighbors = (\n132\t                free_neighbors_by_cell.get(current, ())\n133\t                if free_neighbors_by_cell is not None\n134\t                else _cell_neighbors(current)\n135\t            )\n136\t            for neighbor in neighbors:\n137\t                if neighbor not in free_cells or neighbor in component_by_cell:\n138\t                    continue\n139\t                component_by_cell[neighbor] = component_id\n140\t                component_cells.add(neighbor)\n141\t                stack.append(neighbor)\n142\t        cells_by_component[component_id] = component_cells\n143\t        component_id += 1\n144\t\n145\t    return component_by_cell, cells_by_component\n146\t\n147\t\n148\tdef _peel_terminal_core(\n149\t    component_cells: Set[Tuple[int, int]],\n150\t    terminal_cells: Set[Tuple[int, int]],\n151\t    *,\n152\t    free_neighbors_by_cell: Optional[Mapping[Tuple[int, int], Sequence[Tuple[int, int]]]] = None,\n153\t) -> Set[Tuple[int, int]]:\n154\t    if not component_cells:\n155\t        return set()\n156\t\n157\t    neighbor_map: Dict[Tuple[int, int], Set[Tuple[int, int]]] = {}\n158\t    degree: Dict[Tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n159\t    for cell in component_cells:\n160\t        base_neighbors = (\n161\t            free_neighbors_by_cell.get(cell, ())\n162\t            if free_neighbors_by_cell is not None\n163\t            else _cell_neighbors(cell)\n164\t        )\n165\t        neighbors = {neighbor for neighbor in base_neighbors if neighbor in component_cells}\n166\t        neighbor_map[cell] = neighbors\n167\t        degree[cell] = len(neighbors)\n168\t\n169\t    removed: Set[Tuple[int, int]] = set()\n170\t    queue = deque(\n171\t        cell\n172\t        for cell in component_cells\n173\t        if cell not in terminal_cells and degree.get(cell, 0) < 2\n174\t    )\n175\t    while queue:\n176\t        cell = queue.popleft()\n177\t        if cell in removed or cell in terminal_cells:\n178\t            continue\n179\t        if degree.get(cell, 0) >= 2:\n180\t            continue\n181\t        removed.add(cell)\n182\t        for neighbor in neighbor_map.get(cell, set()):\n183\t            if neighbor in removed:\n184\t                continue\n185\t            degree[neighbor] = degree.get(neighbor, 0) - 1\n186\t            if neighbor not in terminal_cells and degree.get(neighbor, 0) < 2:\n187\t                queue.append(neighbor)\n188\t\n189\t    return {cell for cell in component_cells if cell not in removed}\n190\t\n191\t\n192\tdef _empty_domain_stats() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n193\t    return {\n194\t        \"commodity_component_cells\": {},\n195\t        \"commodity_active_cells\": {},\n196\t        \"commodity_terminal_cells\": {},\n197\t        \"domain_cells\": 0,\n198\t        \"terminal_core_cells\": 0,\n199\t        \"front_terminal_cells\": 0,\n200\t        \"blocked_ports\": 0,\n201\t        \"disconnected_commodity_count\": 0,\n202\t    }\n203\t\n204\t\n205\tdef _resolve_routing_domain_context(\n206\t    *,\n207\t    grid: Optional[\"RoutingGrid\"] = None,\n208\t    placement_core: Optional[RoutingPlacementCore] = None,\n209\t    port_specs: Optional[Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]] = None,\n210\t    occupied_owner_by_cell: Optional[Mapping[Tuple[int, int], str]] = None,\n211\t) -> Tuple[\n212\t    Optional[\"RoutingGrid\"],\n213\t    List[Dict[str, Any]],\n214\t    Set[Tuple[int, int]],\n215\t    Dict[Tuple[int, int], str],\n216\t    Dict[Tuple[int, int], int],\n217\t    Dict[int, Set[Tuple[int, int]]],\n218\t    Optional[Mapping[Tuple[int, int], Sequence[Tuple[int, int]]]],\n219\t]:\n220\t    resolved_grid = grid\n221\t    resolved_core = placement_core\n222\t    if resolved_grid is None and resolved_core is None:\n223\t        raise ValueError(\"analyze_exact_routing_domain requires either grid or placement_core\")\n224\t\n225\t    if resolved_grid is not None:\n226\t        if resolved_core is None:\n227\t            resolved_core = getattr(resolved_grid, \"placement_core\", None)\n228\t        resolved_port_specs = [dict(spec) for spec in resolved_grid.port_specs]\n229\t    else:\n230\t        resolved_port_specs = [dict(spec) for spec in list(port_specs or [])]\n231\t\n232\t    if resolved_core is not None:\n233\t        owner_map = dict(resolved_core.occupied_owner_by_cell)\n234\t        if occupied_owner_by_cell is not None:\n235\t            owner_map.update(\n236\t                {\n237\t                    (int(cell[0]), int(cell[1])): str(owner)\n238\t                    for cell, owner in dict(occupied_owner_by_cell).items()\n239\t                }\n240\t            )\n241\t        return (\n242\t            resolved_grid,\n243\t            resolved_port_specs,\n244\t            set(resolved_core.free_cells),\n245\t            owner_map,\n246\t            dict(resolved_core.component_by_cell),\n247\t            {\n248\t                int(component_id): set(cells)\n249\t                for component_id, cells in resolved_core.cells_by_component.items()\n250\t            },\n251\t            dict(resolved_core.free_neighbors_by_cell),\n252\t        )\n253\t\n254\t    resolved_free_cells = set(getattr(resolved_grid, \"free_cells\", set()))\n255\t    owner_map = {\n256\t        (int(cell[0]), int(cell[1])): str(owner)\n257\t        for cell, owner in dict(\n258\t            occupied_owner_by_cell\n259\t            if occupied_owner_by_cell is not None\n260\t            else getattr(resolved_grid, \"occupied_owner_by_cell\", {})\n261\t        ).items()\n262\t    }\n263\t    component_by_cell, cells_by_component = _compute_free_components(resolved_free_cells)\n264\t    return (\n265\t        resolved_grid,\n266\t        resolved_port_specs,\n267\t        resolved_free_cells,\n268\t        owner_map,\n269\t        component_by_cell,\n270\t        cells_by_component,\n271\t        None,\n272\t    )\n273\t\n274\t\n275\tdef analyze_exact_routing_domain(\n276\t    grid: Optional[\"RoutingGrid\"] = None,\n277\t    *,\n278\t    placement_core: Optional[RoutingPlacementCore] = None,\n279\t    port_specs: Optional[Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]] = None,"}]},"uuid":"bc4fd891-300f-4265-b394-042b32c4acd4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:38.196Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"268a46e6-7378-4d6f-90cb-6548df9e3013","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
