{"parentUuid":"57b69439-bc52-4517-9f82-5c8d1128b381","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bkx8kNpCSYkAppzXFymz1y","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT OR-tools planar graph routing exploit structure 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP SAT solver for vrp\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/tt6JvoTWTvo\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Search - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"description_or-tools_cp-sat.txt\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_or-tools_cp-sat.txt\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: not all threads are used, why? · Issue #2399 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2399\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found general information about CP-SAT and OR-Tools, including their routing and constraint programming capabilities, but the search results don't contain specific information about \"planar graph routing exploit structure\" from 2024.\n\nThe results show that:\n\n- The CP-SAT solver is architectured around five components, including a clause learning SAT solver as the base layer and a Constraint Programming module with routing constraints above it.\n\n- CP-SAT constraints are focused on specific problems, such as routing or scheduling, but very generic and powerful within their domain.\n\nHowever, the specific topic you're asking about—\"planar graph routing exploit structure\"—doesn't appear in these search results. If you're looking for research, publications, or technical discussions about exploiting planar graph properties in routing problems using CP-SAT, you may want to try a more targeted search with additional keywords (such as specific paper titles, authors, or conference names if you're aware of them).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"65a61fe2-8ae7-401f-8bdf-d62255195fb2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:44.506Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"57b69439-bc52-4517-9f82-5c8d1128b381","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"31fb84ac-6e88-444d-91fc-45c7b8ebeda5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LS2K5HjG8o4XHK18tm4q8n","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"multi-layer grid routing 2-layer planar graph VLSI bridge crossing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Multilayer grid embeddings for VLSI | Algorithmica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01759038\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) VLSI Routing in Multiple Layers using Grid based Routing Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/274002131_VLSI_Routing_in_Multiple_Layers_using_Grid_based_Routing_Algorithms\"},{\"title\":\"Physical Design Flow IV:Routing - VLSI Pro\",\"url\":\"https://vlsi.pro/physical-design-flow-iv-routing/\"},{\"title\":\"VLSI Routing in Multiple Layers using Grid based Routing Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcaonline.org/archives/volume93/number16/16303-6210/\"},{\"title\":\"Graph Algorithms for VLSI Power and Clock Networks\",\"url\":\"https://www.hajim.rochester.edu/ece/sites/friedman/Rassul_Bairamkulov_PhD.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Input sensitive VLSI layouts for graphs of arbitrary degree | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/BFb0040394\"},{\"title\":\"Digital VLSI Design Lecture 9: Routing\",\"url\":\"https://enicslabs.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Lecture-9-Routing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"What is detailed Routing in VLSI Physical Design? ~ TechSimplifiedTV.in\",\"url\":\"https://www.techsimplifiedtv.in/2025/04/what-is-detailed-routing-in-vlsi.html\"},{\"title\":\"VLSI Routing in Multiple Layers using Grid based ...\",\"url\":\"https://research.ijcaonline.org/volume93/number16/pxc3896210.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Routing Algorithms for VLSI Design\",\"url\":\"https://web.eecs.umich.edu/~mazum/ClassDescriptions/Routing.pdf\"}]\n\nI've successfully performed the web search for your query on multi-layer grid routing, 2-layer planar graphs, and VLSI bridge crossing. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Research Results:\n\n**Multilayer Grid Embeddings for VLSI:**\nThe research proposes multilayer grid models for VLSI layout that account for the number of contact cuts used, proving a tight area × (number of contact cuts) = Θ(n²) tradeoff for embedding n-node planar graphs of bounded degree in two layers. Any n-node graph of thickness 2 can be embedded on two layers in O(n²) area.\n\n**Multi-Layer Grid Routing Algorithms:**\nRecent research describes multi-layer grid routing algorithms that address the global routing problem of selecting a maximum set of nets such that every net can be routed entirely in one of the given layers without violating physical capacity constraints. These algorithms provide results guaranteed to be within a certain range of the global optimal solution and run in polynomial-time.\n\n**Grid-Based Routing in VLSI:**\nMost routers available are grid based routers with routing grids defined for the entire layout. In two-layer routing, one layer is reserved for horizontal tracks while the other layer is reserved for vertical tracks.\n\nThe search results contain academic research on multi-layer planar graph embeddings and grid-based routing algorithms for VLSI design, with emphasis on area efficiency and optimization of routing across multiple metal layers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c37ec9eb-e328-4587-9f13-e9e94d11b4c3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:47.671Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"31fb84ac-6e88-444d-91fc-45c7b8ebeda5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
