{"parentUuid":"a61c2af3-b566-4ab4-8ab4-30dd34506708","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HUdkhkwz1Hq9icYfRB11MF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"igraph python planar graph algorithms 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"igraph.Graph\",\"url\":\"https://python.igraph.org/en/main/api/igraph.Graph.html\"},{\"title\":\"Tutorial\",\"url\":\"https://igraph.org/python/tutorial/0.9.9/tutorial.html\"},{\"title\":\"Python igraph documentation\",\"url\":\"https://igraph.org/python/\"},{\"title\":\"Visualisation of graphs\",\"url\":\"https://igraph.org/python/tutorial/0.9.6/visualisation.html\"},{\"title\":\"python-igraph API reference\",\"url\":\"https://igraph.org/python/api/latest/igraph.layout.Layout.html\"},{\"title\":\"NetworkX - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NetworkX\"},{\"title\":\"Graph analysis\",\"url\":\"https://igraph.org/python/tutorial/0.9.7/analysis.html\"},{\"title\":\"python-igraph · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/python-igraph/\"},{\"title\":\"Tutorial — igraph 1.0.0 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://python.igraph.org/en/main/tutorial.html\"},{\"title\":\"Network Analysis Using Igraph — Python Notes for Linguistics\",\"url\":\"https://alvinntnu.github.io/python-notes/statistical-analyses/network-analysis-igraph.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about igraph, Python, and planar graph algorithms:\n\n## igraph Python Library Overview\n\nigraph is a Python interface to the igraph high performance graph library, primarily aimed at complex network research and analysis. igraph enables analysis of graphs/networks from simple operations such as adding and removing nodes to complex theoretical constructs such as community detection.\n\n## Layout and Planar Graph Support\n\nWhile the search results don't specifically detail dedicated planar graph algorithms within igraph itself, the results do show that igraph implements quite a few layout algorithms and is also able to draw them onto the screen or to a PDF, PNG or SVG file using the Cairo library.\n\nFor reference, the search results mention that other libraries like NetworkX do support planar graph operations. Planar layout attempts to compute an embedding for planar graphs (graphs with no edge crossings) using graph combinatorial embedding. If the graph isn't planar, it raises an exception. Planar embeddings exactly preserve the topology of planar networks—useful for circuit schematics, maps, or any truly planar structure.\n\n## Current State (2024)\n\nAs of April 2024, NetworkX had over 50 million downloads, surpassing the download count of the second most popular package, igraph, by more than 50-fold.\n\nIf you need more specific information about particular planar graph algorithms in igraph or recent 2024 updates, I'd recommend checking the official igraph Python documentation directly at python.igraph.org.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"62eee8e8-c3df-422e-9a6e-02ab2716c34b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:00.757Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a61c2af3-b566-4ab4-8ab4-30dd34506708","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ef88a154-90ee-4900-ba95-411fc4b455b5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0179qbcFis2FF5UM2opVMpPE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"planar separator\" \"Benders\" decomposition speedup empirical\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Benders Decomposition Approach for Generalized Maximal Covering and Partial Set Covering Location Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2073-8994/17/9/1417\"},{\"title\":\"Engineering planar separator algorithms | ACM Journal of Experimental Algorithmics\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/1498698.1571635\"},{\"title\":\"Robust Critical Node Selection by Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/4012.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Engineering Planar Separator Algorithms | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/11561071_56\"},{\"title\":\"Planar separator theorem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planar_separator_theorem\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerating Benders decomposition for solving a sequence of sample average approximation replicationsThis research has been supported by ONR grant N00014-21-1-2574.\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2411.09091v1\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) The Benders Decomposition Algorithm: A Literature Review\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/305218145_The_Benders_Decomposition_Algorithm_A_Literature_Review\"},{\"title\":\"Multicut Benders decomposition algorithm for process supply chain planning under uncertainty | Annals of Operations Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-011-0974-4\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerating logic-based Benders decomposition for railway rescheduling by exploiting similarities in delays - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054822003057\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - JuMP-dev\",\"url\":\"https://jump.dev/JuMP.jl/stable/tutorials/algorithms/benders_decomposition/\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about planar separators and Benders decomposition. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Planar Separator Algorithms\n\nClassical linear-time planar separator algorithms determine for a given planar graph a small subset of its nodes whose removal divides the graph into two components of similar size, based on planar separator theorems which guarantee separators of size O(√n) and remaining components of size at most 2n/3.\n\nA comprehensive experimental study of planar separator algorithms on a large variety of graphs has been conducted, with the goal of finding separators that possess desirable qualities with respect to separator size and component balance. The use of fundamental cycles, whose size is at most twice the diameter of the graph, as planar separators was proposed, and for graphs of small diameter this strategy outperformed other algorithms.\n\n## Benders Decomposition Speedup\n\nRegarding empirical speedup results with Benders decomposition:\n\n- Computational experiments on large-scale synthetic instances with up to 200,000 demand points demonstrate that a Benders decomposition method attained more than a threefold speedup over CPLEX.\n\n- For instances with planar graphs, a proposed Benders approach remained very efficient, solving all instances to optimality within an average computational time of 8.1 seconds for problems with 100 vertices and 118 seconds for problems with 200 vertices.\n\nThe search results show successful applications of both planar separators and Benders decomposition, but don't appear to contain research specifically combining these two concepts.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a6261f60-f2dc-4ace-977d-41047d3179bd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:02.329Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ef88a154-90ee-4900-ba95-411fc4b455b5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a6261f60-f2dc-4ace-977d-41047d3179bd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01AeZiXvntP3LkL795sLFEeB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material now. Let me check one more thing — the actual structure of the routing graph (layers + bridges = does this break planarity?)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2875,"cache_read_input_tokens":39415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2875,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozhXmdJP2k1WwPGT2eX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"785afd56-a5be-4418-a25e-443daeb16671","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:06.325Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"785afd56-a5be-4418-a25e-443daeb16671","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01AeZiXvntP3LkL795sLFEeB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BuKNVtMqnQCTPTdeaPPmNq","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\src\\models\\routing_subproblem.py","offset":820,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2875,"cache_read_input_tokens":39415,"output_tokens":176,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2875},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":176,"cache_read_input_tokens":39415,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2875,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2875,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozhXmdJP2k1WwPGT2eX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6711edab-ee17-428e-bc4c-81f6e1545d0e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:07.370Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6711edab-ee17-428e-bc4c-81f6e1545d0e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BuKNVtMqnQCTPTdeaPPmNq","type":"tool_result","content":"820\t            \"local_pattern_pruned_states\": int(local_pattern_pruned_states),\n821\t            \"naive_full_domain_vars\": int(naive_full_domain_vars),\n822\t        }\n823\t\n824\t    def _add_obstacle_exclusion(self):\n825\t        # Obstacle exclusion is implemented by only creating variables on active free cells.\n826\t        return\n827\t\n828\t    def _add_capacity_constraints(self):\n829\t        for vars_on_cell_layer in self._vars_by_cell_layer.values():\n830\t            if vars_on_cell_layer:\n831\t                self.model.AddAtMostOne(vars_on_cell_layer)\n832\t\n833\t    def _add_bridge_constraints(self):\n834\t        for cell, l1_vars in self._l1_vars.items():\n835\t            if not l1_vars:\n836\t                continue\n837\t            l0_nonstraight = self._l0_nonstraight_vars.get(cell, [])\n838\t            if not l0_nonstraight:\n839\t                continue\n840\t            x, y = cell\n841\t            l1_any = self.model.NewBoolVar(f\"l1_any_{x}_{y}\")\n842\t            self.model.AddMaxEquality(l1_any, l1_vars)\n843\t            for var in l0_nonstraight:\n844\t                self.model.AddImplication(l1_any, var.Not())\n845\t\n846\t    def _add_continuity_constraints(self):\n847\t        for commodity in self.commodities:\n848\t            for (x, y) in self._commodity_active_cells.get(commodity, set()):\n849\t                for layer in LAYERS:\n850\t                    for d_out in DIRECTIONS:\n851\t                        self._add_successor_constraints(x, y, layer, d_out, commodity)\n852\t                    for d_in in DIRECTIONS:\n853\t                        self._add_predecessor_constraints(x, y, layer, d_in, commodity)\n854\t\n855\t    def _add_successor_constraints(\n856\t        self,\n857\t        x: int,\n858\t        y: int,\n859\t        layer: int,\n860\t        d_out: str,\n861\t        commodity: str,\n862\t    ) -> None:\n863\t        out_vars = self._vars_by_cell_layer_dir_out_commodity.get((x, y, layer, d_out, commodity), [])\n864\t        if not out_vars:\n865\t            return\n866\t\n867\t        if layer == GROUND_LAYER and self._sink_port_fronts.get((x, y, d_out, commodity), 0) > 0:\n868\t            return\n869\t\n870\t        dx, dy = DIR_DELTA[d_out]\n871\t        nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n872\t        if (nx, ny) not in self._commodity_active_cells.get(commodity, set()):\n873\t            for var in out_vars:\n874\t                self.model.Add(var == 0)\n875\t            return\n876\t\n877\t        recv_dir = DIR_OPP[d_out]\n878\t        recv_vars = self._vars_by_cell_dir_in_commodity.get((nx, ny, recv_dir, commodity), [])\n879\t        if not recv_vars:"}]},"uuid":"17d1755e-7ba4-455a-9e27-38c69d0c88ca","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:07.381Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6711edab-ee17-428e-bc4c-81f6e1545d0e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"17d1755e-7ba4-455a-9e27-38c69d0c88ca","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a5ed0a16a983cc48c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HTTvHUyUYEkGP6FpNLapFP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good, I have what I need. Confirmed: 2-layer (ground + elevated) with bridges, plus multiple commodities. Now let me write the analysis.\n\n---\n\n# 调研：planar graph 算法在 70×70 grid placement 上的可借鉴性\n\n## 1. Lipton-Tarjan planar separator 现代实现\n\n经典定理：n 顶点平面图可在 O(n) 时间分成 A、B、C 三块，C 是大小 O(√n) 的分隔集，A、B 各 ≤ 2n/3。\n\n**现成实现：**\n- `jeffythedragonslayer/lipton-tarjan` (C++/BGL)\n- `ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan` (Python，纯学术，性能未优化)\n- OGDF (C++ 库) 有专业的 `Planar Separator Algorithms` 模块，含多种变体\n- Sariel Har-Peled 2025 教材给出现代化讲解\n\n**实测经验** (Holzer 等 ACM JEA 2009 \"Engineering planar separator algorithms\")：基于 fundamental cycles 的简单算法在小直径图上经常打败 Lipton-Tarjan 原版。70×70 网格直径 ≈ 140，属于\"中等\"，不算最有利场景。\n\n## 2. Planar multi-commodity flow 算法\n\n经典结果：\n- Matsumoto-Nishizeki-Saito (1985)：源汇都在外面的 planar undirected MCF，O(kn + n²√log n)\n- Borradaile-Klein 2009：单源单汇 max-flow 在 directed planar 上 O(n log n)，是教科书结果\n- 2023 (Combinatorica)：acyclic planar digraph 上 integer multiflow，O((R+1)^(4k²) k³ n) — k 是 commodity 数；**指数依赖 k**，对我们多 commodity 场景几乎无用\n\n**关键限制：** 这些算法基本都要求\"所有 source/sink 都在外面\" (boundary of infinite face) 或者其他强结构假设。我们的 ports 散布在 grid 内部各处，**不满足**。\n\n## 3. Grid graph 专用算法\n\nChuzhoy-Kim-Li 等近年关于 NDP (node-disjoint paths) on grids 的工作：grid 上 NDP 仍是 NP-hard 且 APX-hard，最佳上界 Õ(n^¼) 近似。**精确求解没有比一般 planar 更快的多项式算法。**\n\n也就是说：grid 的\"额外结构\"对**判定/优化**类的 routing/disjoint paths 问题没给精确算法上的便宜，只在**近似**和**布局/嵌入**问题上有。\n\n## 4. CP-SAT 是否已识别 planar 结构\n\nOR-Tools CP-SAT 没有任何 planar-graph-aware 的内部传播器。它把所有约束当通用 CP/SAT 处理。它的强项是 lazy clause learning + LNS + presolve，**不会从图的平面性中得到额外加速**。\n(d-krupke/cpsat-primer 文档明确：CP-SAT 的图相关原语只有 `AddCircuit`、`AddMultipleCircuit`，没有 planar separator。)\n\n## 5. NetworkX / igraph / OGDF 工具链\n\n- **NetworkX 3.6**：`check_planarity`、`PlanarEmbedding`、`combinatorial_embedding_to_pos`，**没有 separator 算法、没有 planar max-flow**\n- **igraph**：planar 仅限 layout，无算法\n- **OGDF**：唯一有完整 planar separator 实现的库，但 C++ 为主，`ogdf-python` 走 cppyy 绑定，集成成本高（需要本地 shared lib build）\n\n## 6. 我们的 routing/flow 真的 planar 吗？\n\n**不严格 planar。** 三个破坏点：\n\n1. **2 层结构**：`GROUND_LAYER + ELEVATED_LAYER`，bridge 允许 elevated 跨过 ground。这就是 thickness-2 graph，**严格意义不是 planar**（虽然每层单独 planar）。Multilayer grid embedding 文献 (Springer 1990) 处理过这种情况，但没有 √n 加速结论。\n2. **多 commodity**：每条 commodity 独立的 routing 变量在 CP-SAT 里通过 capacity (`AddAtMostOne` per cell-layer) 耦合 — 这是约束图，不是物理图。物理 grid 是 planar，但 CP-SAT 看到的\"变量交互图\"远不是。\n3. **Port 端口**：port 节点接到 grid 内部 cell 的多个方向，并且 binding subproblem 把不同 instance 的 port 通过 commodity 全局耦合。这些跨距离耦合再次破坏 planarity。\n\n`flow_subproblem.py` 的诊断 LP 单层 cell-graph **是** planar — 但它只是诊断器，不参与正式剪枝。\n\n## 7. 工程成本\n\n要落地任何 planar 加速：\n- 集成 OGDF (~1-2 周)：搭建 cppyy + shared lib，包装 Python API\n- 把 routing 状态空间映射成 planar separator 可消化的图：**根本不存在干净映射**，因为状态变量是 (cell, layer, in_dirs, out_dirs, commodity)，不是图节点\n- Benders cut 生成里塞 separator-based 分解：理论上可以做\"按 √n 分隔切空间\"的 master，但需要从头设计 cut 语义，而且没有现成证据说在 70×70 这个规模 (n=4900) 上 √n ≈ 70 的加速能 cover 解码开销\n\n## 是否任何 planar 加速对 routing 有用\n\n**结论：基本无用，不推荐投入。**\n\n三条决定性理由：\n\n1. **物理 planar ≠ 求解器看到的 planar**。CP-SAT routing 的耦合图（变量约束图）因多 commodity、多层桥、port 全局绑定，已经不是 planar。Lipton-Tarjan 切的是物理图，对求解器搜索空间没意义。\n2. **70×70 规模太小**。√n=70，O(n log n) 与 O(n) 对 n=4900 基本无差异。Borradaile-Klein 这种渐近优势的常数项很重，工程实现一般要 n ≥ 10⁵ 才看得出收益。我们一次 Benders 迭代花在 routing CP-SAT 上的时间，远不是被图算法常数项卡住的。\n3. **没有现成 path**。OGDF 是唯一可用引擎，但绑定成本（1-2 周）拿来对一个不严格 planar 的子问题做\"或许有用\"的加速，期望 ROI 远低于现有 lane B (deterministic tuning) 和 lane C (AI sidecar) 的已知收益。\n\n如果非要找个 planar 算法的小用法，**唯一可能的轻量切入点**是：把 `flow_subproblem.py` 的诊断 LP（单层、纯 cell graph、确实 planar）从通用 LP 换成 Borradaile-Klein 风格 max-flow，但这是诊断器不在 hot path 上，加速也只对极个别 candidate 触发。**不值得做。**\n\n建议归档为 \"investigated, not pursued\"，不进 Phase 3C 路线图。\n\n**Sources:**\n- [Planar separator theorem - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planar_separator_theorem)\n- [Sariel Har-Peled 2025 chapter](https://sarielhp.org/book/chapters/separator.pdf)\n- [OGDF Planar Separator Algorithms](https://ogdf.github.io/doc/ogdf/group__ga-plansep.html)\n- [ogdf-python bindings](https://github.com/ogdf/ogdf-python)\n- [jeffythedragonslayer/lipton-tarjan C++ impl](https://github.com/jeffythedragonslayer/lipton-tarjan)\n- [ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan Python impl](https://github.com/ValeryTyumen/lipton_tarjan)\n- [Borradaile-Klein O(n log n) max st-flow](https://www.cs.uoi.gr/~loukas/courses/grad/Algorithmic_Graph_Theory/index.files/a9-borradaile.pdf)\n- [Integer Multiflows in Acyclic Planar Digraphs (Combinatorica 2023)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00493-023-00065-0)\n- [Almost Polynomial Hardness of NDP in Grids](https://theoryofcomputing.org/articles/v017a006/)\n- [Improved Approximation Algorithm for NDP in Grid (Chuzhoy)](https://home.ttic.edu/~cjulia/papers/NDP-in-grids-alg-full.pdf)\n- [Engineering planar separator algorithms (ACM JEA)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/1498698.1571635)\n- [NetworkX Planarity docs](https://networkx.org/documentation/stable/reference/algorithms/planarity.html)\n- [Multilayer grid embeddings for VLSI (Algorithmica)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01759038)\n- [CP-SAT Primer - Advanced Modeling](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_read_input_tokens":42290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1222,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozhudmTt1Ew1po9gHqB","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"841a49e2-720b-4bc9-87b3-fe0511aa14a2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:28:12.711Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
